  "claim": "The TV show starring an actor was written by the creator of the radio talk show \"The Borowitz Report\". This show also starred Joseph Marcell as the butler. The first actor also stars in the 2019 film Aladdin.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Andy Borowitz. Sentence: Andy Borowitz (born January 4, 1958) is an American writer, comedian, satirist, and actor.\nPage: Andy Borowitz. Sentence: He is known for creating \"The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air\" and the satirical column \"The Borowitz Report\".\nPage: The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air. Sentence: The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air is an American sitcom that originally aired on NBC from September 10, 1990, to May 20, 1996.\nPage: The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air. Sentence: The show stars Will Smith as a fictionalized version of himself, a street-smart teenager from West Philadelphia who is sent to move in with his wealthy aunt and uncle in their Bel Air mansion after getting into a fight on a local basketball court.\nPage: Joseph Marcell. Sentence: Joseph Marcell (born 18 August 1948) is a Saint Lucian born British actor, best known for his role as Geoffrey the butler on the NBC sitcom \"The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air\" from September 1990, until it ended in May 1996.\nPage: Aladdin (2019 film). Sentence: The film stars Mena Massoud as the titular character with Naomi Scott, Will Smith, Marwan Kenzari, Navid Negahban, Nasim Pedrad, Billy Magnussen, and Numan Acar in supporting roles.",
